 "literal": "Heated on-the-back old-chameleon male / path-traversing people omen-to-take waiting / to-the-desert-indeed went lover, losing-my-strength / here-I endured grief / how did-it-know this clamorous-town-indeed?",
 "translation": "My lover has departed into the desert where an old male chameleon with a sun-heated back waits to be taken as an omen by travelers on the path. My strength having completely failed me, how did this gossiping, clamorous town find out about the secret grief I endure here?",
 "modern": "சூடான முதுகை உடைய ஓதி எனப்படும் பல்லியின் முதிர்ந்த ஆண், வழியில் செல்லும் மக்கள் சகுனமாகப் பார்க்கும்படி காத்திருக்கும் பாலைவனத்திற்கு என் காதலர் சென்றுவிட்டார். என் மனவலிமை அழிந்துபோக, இங்கு நான் தாங்கிக்கொண்டிருக்கும் துன்பத்தை இந்த ஆரவாரமிக்க ஊர் எவ்வாறு அறிந்துகொண்டது?",
 "explanation": "The heroine speaks to her close friend (tōḻi) or to herself in distress after her lover has departed for the desert (pālai) to earn wealth. She describes the harsh desert landscape where an old male chameleon sits with its back heated by the sun, serving as an omen (puḷ) for travelers. The image of the chameleon waiting passively on the path reflects her own state of waiting in agony. She laments that her inner strength has completely collapsed under the weight of separation. Finally, she wonders with frustration how the gossiping, noisy town has already found out about her hidden grief, as they have begun to spread rumors about her state.",
